  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Grith">Grið</ref> 2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2" corresp="#wit-g-b"><pb n="470" ed="#liebermann"/>Ðon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> is rihtlic, þ<hi rend="italic">æt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Grith_2.lnote.oe.2"/></hi> Godes cyricgrið<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Grith_2.lnote.oe.3"/> binnan wagum ⁊ Cristenes cyninges handgrið stande efen unwe<hi rend="italic">m</hi>me.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" n="2" corresp="#wit-g-b"><pb n="22" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Ðonne is rihtlic þæt Godes cyricgrið binnan wagum and Cristenes cyninges handgrið stande efen unwemme.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="470" ed="#liebermann"/>Nun ist rechtmässig, dass der von Gottes Kirche innerhalb ihrer Mauern [ausgehende] Sonderfriede und der Sonderfriede aus der Hand des christlichen Königs gleichermassen unverletzlich bestehe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Now it is lawful that the special peace [proceeding] from God's church within its walls and the special peace from the hand of the Christian king should stand equally inviolable.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-b"><pb n="23" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Therefore, it is right that the sanctuary within the walls of God’s church and the sanctuary received from the hand of a Christian king remain equally inviolable.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="470"><ref target="clause:ICn_2-2">I Cn 2.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 2, 2</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><ref target="clause:ICn_2-2">I Cn 2.2</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares I Cn 2.2.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Grith_2.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">470</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">⁊ <hi rend="italic">Wilkins Thorpe</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">⁊ Wilkins Thorpe</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Grith_2.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">470</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">i <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> y <hi rend="italic">Thorpe</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">i instead of y Thorpe</seg></note>
      </div>
